                    "page_content='On this page\n          \n\n\n\n\nOpik\nOpik\nOpik.__init__()\nOpik.config\nOpik.rest_client\nOpik.project_name\nOpik.auth_check()\nOpik.trace()\nOpik.copy_traces()\nOpik.span()\nOpik.update_span()\nOpik.log_spans_feedback_scores()\nOpik.log_traces_feedback_scores()\nOpik.delete_trace_feedback_score()\nOpik.delete_span_feedback_score()\nOpik.get_dataset()\nOpik.get_datasets()\nOpik.get_dataset_experiments()\nOpik.delete_dataset()\nOpik.create_dataset()\nOpik.get_or_create_dataset()\nOpik.create_experiment()\nOpik.get_experiment_by_name()\nOpik.get_experiments_by_name()\nOpik.get_experiment_by_id()\nOpik.end()\nOpik.flush()\nOpik.search_traces()\nOpik.search_spans()\nOpik.get_trace_content()\nOpik.get_span_content()\nOpik.get_project()\nOpik.get_project_url()\nOpik.get_threads_client()\nOpik.get_attachment_client()\nOpik.create_prompt()\nOpik.get_prompt()\nOpik.get_all_prompts()\nOpik.create_optimization()\nOpik.delete_optimizations()\nOpik.get_optimization_by_id()' metadata={'language': 'en', 'title': 'Opik - opik', 'content_type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', 'source': 'https://www.comet.com/docs/opik/python-sdk-reference/Opik.html'}",
                    "page_content='to use. You can pass \"native\" which will log all output even when it originated from a C native library. You can also pass \"simple\" which will work only for output made by Python code. If you want to disable automatic output logging, you can pass False. The default is \"simple\".auto_log_co2 (bool, default: True ) â€“ Automatically tracks the CO2 emission of this experiment if codecarbon package is installed in the environmentparse_args (bool, default: True ) â€“ Allows you to enable/disable automatic parsing of CLI argumentslog_env_details (bool, default: True ) â€“ Log various environment information in order to identify where the script is runninglog_env_gpu (bool, default: True ) â€“ Allow you to enable/disable the automatic collection of gpu details and metrics (utilization, memory usage etc..). log_env_details must also be true.log_env_cpu (bool, default: True ) â€“ Allow you to enable/disable the automatic collection of cpu details and metrics (utilization, memory usage etc..).' metadata={'language': 'en', 'source': 'https://www.comet.com/docs/v2/api-and-sdk/python-sdk/reference/Experiment/', 'description': 'Supercharging Machine Learning', 'title': 'Experiment - Comet Docs', 'content_type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8'}",
                    "page_content='id – The unique identifier for the trace, if not provided, a new ID will be generated. Must be a valid [UUIDv7](https://uuid7.com/) ID.\nname – The name of the trace.\nstart_time – The start time of the trace. If not provided, the current local time will be used.\nend_time – The end time of the trace.\ninput – The input data for the trace. This can be any valid JSON serializable object.\noutput – The output data for the trace. This can be any valid JSON serializable object.\nmetadata – Additional metadata for the trace. This can be any valid JSON serializable object.\ntags – Tags associated with the trace.\nfeedback_scores – The list of feedback score dicts associated with the trace. Dicts don’t require to have an id value.\nproject_name – The name of the project. If not set, the project name which was configured when Opik instance\nwas created will be used.\nerror_info – The dictionary with error information (typically used when the trace function has failed).' metadata={'title': 'Opik - opik', 'language': 'en', 'content_type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', 'source': 'https://www.comet.com/docs/opik/python-sdk-reference/Opik.html'}",
