                        "page_content='On this page\n          \n\n\n\n\nOpik\nOpik\nOpik.__init__()\nOpik.config\nOpik.rest_client\nOpik.project_name\nOpik.auth_check()\nOpik.trace()\nOpik.copy_traces()\nOpik.span()\nOpik.update_span()\nOpik.log_spans_feedback_scores()\nOpik.log_traces_feedback_scores()\nOpik.delete_trace_feedback_score()\nOpik.delete_span_feedback_score()\nOpik.get_dataset()\nOpik.get_datasets()\nOpik.get_dataset_experiments()\nOpik.delete_dataset()\nOpik.create_dataset()\nOpik.get_or_create_dataset()\nOpik.create_experiment()\nOpik.get_experiment_by_name()\nOpik.get_experiments_by_name()\nOpik.get_experiment_by_id()\nOpik.end()\nOpik.flush()\nOpik.search_traces()\nOpik.search_spans()\nOpik.get_trace_content()\nOpik.get_span_content()\nOpik.get_project()\nOpik.get_project_url()\nOpik.get_threads_client()\nOpik.get_attachment_client()\nOpik.create_prompt()\nOpik.get_prompt()\nOpik.get_all_prompts()\nOpik.create_optimization()\nOpik.delete_optimizations()\nOpik.get_optimization_by_id()' metadata={'title': 'Opik - opik', 'source': 'https://www.comet.com/docs/opik/python-sdk-reference/Opik.html', 'language': 'en', 'content_type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8'}",
                        "page_content='Parameters:\n\nproject_name – The name of the project. If not provided, traces and spans will be logged to the Default Project.\nworkspace – The name of the workspace. If not provided, default will be used.\nhost – The host URL for the Opik server. If not provided, it will default to https://www.comet.com/opik/api.\napi_key – The API key for Opik. This parameter is ignored for local installations.\n_use_batching – intended for internal usage in specific conditions only.\nEnabling it is unsafe and can lead to data loss.\n_show_misconfiguration_message – intended for internal usage in specific conditions only.\nPrint a warning message if the Opik server is not configured properly.\n\n\nReturns:\nNone\n\n\n\n\n\nproperty config: OpikConfig¶\nReturns:\nconfig.OpikConfig: Read-only copy of the configuration of the Opik client.' metadata={'language': 'en', 'title': 'Opik - opik', 'source': 'https://www.comet.com/docs/opik/python-sdk-reference/Opik.html', 'content_type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8'}",
                        "page_content='Returns:\nNone\n\n\n\n\n\nproperty config: OpikConfig¶\nReturns:\nconfig.OpikConfig: Read-only copy of the configuration of the Opik client.\n\n\n\nproperty rest_client: OpikApi¶\nProvides direct access to the underlying REST API client.\nWARNING: This client is not guaranteed to be backward compatible with future SDK versions.\nWhile it provides a convenient way to use the current REST API of Opik.\nHowever, it’s not considered safe to heavily rely on its API as Opik’s REST API contracts may change.\n\nReturns:\nThe REST client used by the Opik client.\n\nReturn type:\nOpikApi\n\n\n\n\n\nproperty project_name: str¶\nThis property retrieves the name of the project associated with the instance.\nIt is a read-only property.\n\nReturns:\nThe name of the project.\n\nReturn type:\nstr\n\n\n\n\n\nauth_check() → None¶\nChecks if current API key user has an access to the configured workspace and its content.' metadata={'language': 'en', 'content_type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', 'title': 'Opik - opik', 'source': 'https://www.comet.com/docs/opik/python-sdk-reference/Opik.html'}"
