                {
                    "role": "system",
                    "content": "Provide an answer to the question. \n\n## Examples\n- Question: `What is the purpose of the `opik.configure()` function in the Opik Python SDK?`\n  Answer: `The `configure()` function initializes the SDK, allowing you to set up connectivity to the Opik backend (e.g. by specifying `use_local`).`\n\n\n- Question: `What is the role of the `Prompt` class in the Python SDK?`\n  Answer: `The `Prompt` class provides prompt management capabilities, allowing you to define and reuse prompt templates.`\n\n\n- Question: `How do you mark a function to automatically log traces in Opik using the Python SDK?`\n  Answer: `Use the `track` decorator provided by Opik to wrap your function so that its LLM calls and context get automatically logged.`\n\n\n- Question: `How do you mark a function to automatically log traces in Opik using the Python SDK?`\n  Answer: `Use the `track` decorator provided by Opik to wrap your function so that its LLM calls and context get automatically logged.`\n\n\n- Question: `Which testing utility does Opik offer to support unit testing of LLMs in the SDK?`\n  Answer: `Opik provides the `llm_unit` testing utility to support LLM unit-testing workflows.`\n\n\n- Question: `Name three built-in evaluation metrics that the Opik Python SDK includes.`\n  Answer: `Examples include `Hallucination`, `AnswerRelevance`, and `ContextPrecision`, among others.`\n\n\n- Question: `How does Opik support managing evaluation datasets via the Python SDK?`\n  Answer: `The Opik class provides a `Dataset` object to create or access evaluation datasets programmatically.`\n"
                },
                {
                    "role": "user",
                    "content": "If you want to evaluate a prompt with certain inputs and metrics, which method should you use?"
                }
